mmon  interest so typically you know the  health sector works individually and  education sector works individually this  was a policy that brought together  government non-government development  partners but not just at a central level  there was also sort of a a vertical  level of contribution with provincial  partners their district level partners  there so in terms of the process this  was a very unique conversation that had  occurred and it was sort of remarked on  and used as a model for other policies  that are being developed the next piece  of this that has actually been very  fabulous is the country now is  developing a very detailed plan of  action so the policies are the broad  statement of where the country wants to  go in terms of improving children's  lives in terms of getting to healthy  citizenry mmm-hmm the country now has  decided that they want a detailed plan  that breaks it up here by your step by  step with accountabilities withdrawals  responsibilities with funds being  allocated to expansion of kindergarten  programs expansion of community-based  programs scaling up of immunization  program so we're seeing many different  directions in which now there are  detailed steps being outlined to move  this forward it's wonderful in terms  let's go back to the global policy I'm  very curious to know so there's a global  policy but there's so many countries at  in the developing world of at different  levels of development how does that work  to have a global policy and then  implement it at the national level  so there isn't one I guess I should  start by saying that isn't one global  policy okay and with respect to young  children really who we're talking about  is children prenatally to about eight  years of age and we're not just talking  about the growing child we're talking  about the context around the child the  services that the child receives the the  programs and provisions that enhance the  development of human potential so in  order to 